Description: runtime and shims to run Granola on Linux
 Granola is a meeting notepad: it records a call, transcribes it and drafts the
 notes. Its makers publish builds for macOS and Windows only. This package
 supplies what the macOS build needs in order to run on Linux, namely the
 Electron runtime it expects, JavaScript stand-ins for the macOS native modules
 it loads, and a SQLite build carrying the two extensions its own fork relies
 on.
 .
 The package does not distribute Granola. On first run it extracts the
 application from the official .dmg downloaded from granola.ai into the user's
 home directory, so nothing proprietary is redistributed here.
 .
 Signing in, recording, live transcription and automatic note generation all
 work. Meeting auto-detection does not, because it relies on a macOS interface
 reporting which applications currently hold the microphone, and no Linux
 equivalent is implemented yet.
